course: dictionary
lesson: 7140
title: The pentagon
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pentagon is a flat shape with 5 straight sides and 5 corners. Penta means five, so when you see a shape with five sides, think pentagon.
explain: Look at this: «repeat 5: move 10, turn right 72» draws a pentagon. Five turns of 72 degrees make 5 × 72 = 360 degrees, a full turn, so the sprite ends where it started.
explain: Pentagon can also be a name. In «The Pentagon is a big five-sided building in the USA where the army leaders work», the capital P and the words "army leaders" show it is a building, not a shape.
fact: A pentagon has 5 sides and 5 corners.
fact: «A triangle has 3 sides and 3 corners, a square 4, a pentagon 5 and a hexagon 6.»
fact: A flat shape has as many corners as sides.
fact: The Pentagon is a big building in the USA where army leaders work.
fact: A soccer ball has pentagons on it, and «home plate» in baseball is a pentagon.
exercise: How many sides does a pentagon have? | 3 | *5 | 4 | 6
exercise: «A triangle has 3 sides and 3 corners, a square 4, a pentagon 5 and a hexagon 6.» Which shape has 6 sides? | *Hexagon | Pentagon | Square | Triangle
exercise: Ali says «the Pentagon» is a shape. What is the Pentagon really? | A type of soccer ball | *A big five-sided building where army leaders work | A flat shape with 5 sides | A kind of starfish
test: «repeat 5: move 10, turn right 72» draws which shape? | Triangle | *Pentagon | Hexagon | Square
test: How many corners does a flat shape with 5 sides have? | *5 | 4 | 10 | 6
exam: Ali says a regular pentagon has equal sides and equal angles. Which is true of a regular pentagon? | *Its sides and angles are all equal | It has 6 corners | It has 4 sides | Its sides are all different lengths
